course: dictionary
lesson: 5960
title: Maternity and paternity
level: primary-6
stars: 1
explain: Maternity is a word about mothers and having babies. As a noun it means the state of being a mother. As an adjective, it goes before another word, like maternity clothes or a maternity ward, and it means to do with having a baby.
explain: Context helps you with this word. «Parents get time off work, called maternity and paternity leave, to look after a new baby.» The words «time off work» and «new baby» tell you that maternity leave is a break from work for a mother who has just had a baby.
explain: Notice the pattern «maternity» and «paternity». The first is for mothers and the second is for fathers. When you learn one, you can often work out the other.
fact: Maternity means the state of being a mother.
fact: «Maternity leave» means time off work that a mother gets before and after her baby is born.
fact: «Maternity pay» is money paid to a mother while she is on maternity leave.
fact: «Hospitals have maternity wards where babies are born.» A maternity ward is a part of a hospital.
fact: The father's version of maternity is «paternity».
exercise: «Parents get time off work, called maternity and paternity leave, to look after a new baby.» What is maternity leave? | Money for buying new clothes | A holiday abroad with the family | *Time off work for a mother around the birth of a baby | Time off school for a child
exercise: «Hospitals have maternity wards where babies are born.» What is a maternity ward? | A ward where mothers are punished | A shop that sells baby clothes | *A part of a hospital where babies are born | A classroom where new teachers learn
exercise: «Maternity leave is time off work for a new mother; in Britain it can last up to a year, often on lower pay.» Copy the word that shows the pay may be less. | new | year | time | *lower
test: Which phrase means clothes for a woman who is going to have a baby? | new clothes for school | paternity leave | *maternity clothes | maternity ward
test: What is the father's version of maternity? | fraternity | sorority | maternal | *paternity
exam: Ella says maternity means having a baby for dads too. Is she right? | Only for fathers | *No, it is about being a mother | Yes, for both parents | Maybe, it depends on the hospital
